## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates system design expertise for real-time, privacy-preserving machine learning at scale, requiring careful balance between latency constraints, hardware heterogeneity, and cross-modal fusion capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Hardware-aware model architecture with mixed-precision optimization
- Early-exit strategies and multi-modal feature fusion
- Dynamic batching and latency budget management
- Federated learning with privacy-preserving updates
- Model drift detection and continuous calibration

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(x){
  const encoder = sharedEncoder(x);
  const confidence = calculateConfidence(encoder);

  if (confidence > threshold) {
    return earlyExit(encoder);
  }

  const features = modalityFusion(encoder);
  return finalClassification(features);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Production anomaly systems face non-stationarity, sparse labels, and strict latency. This question tests end-to-end design, from data schema to deployment, plus practical techniques like self-supervised pretraining and online adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Self-supervised pretraining for unlabeled streams
- Online adaptation with meta-learning
- Two-tower architecture for heterogeneous features
- Drift detection and safe rollout/rollback
- Latency budgeting and quantization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example gating logic for latency-adaptive routing
function route(payload, limitMs) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  const score = computeScore(payload);
  const dt = performance.now() - t0;
  if (dt > limitMs) return 'fallback';
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
